# Leave commits to the user

Do not run `git commit`, a `git merge` that creates a commit, `git commit --amend`, or `git push`.

Finish the work and leave it in the working tree. Say that it is ready to commit. Do not stage unless asked.

```
git merge --no-commit origin/some-branch
```

A later message that explicitly tells you to create the commit overrides this for that commit only.
